# Code in Documents
## Single blocks and multi-language tabs

## A Single Code Block

```go
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
	fmt.Println("Hello, ZiraDocs!")
}
```

## Code Groups — Tabs for Multiple Languages

::::code-group
```go [fibonacci.go]
func fibonacci(n int) int {
	if n <= 1 {
		return n
	}
	return fibonacci(n-1) + fibonacci(n-2)
}
```

```python [fibonacci.py]
def fibonacci(n):
    if n <= 1:
        return n
    return fibonacci(n - 1) + fibonacci(n - 2)
```

```typescript [fibonacci.ts]
function fibonacci(n: number): number {
  if (n <= 1) return n;
  return fibonacci(n - 1) + fibonacci(n - 2);
}
```
:::

## Wrap-Up

::: tip
Code groups are great for showing the same idea across languages, or a
"config, then usage" pair, without splitting one explanation across
several sections. They render the same in every output format —
`--format html`, `--format pdf`, `--format docx`, and `--format markdown`.
:::
